 # xv6 NIC Driver Project
+
 This project implements a network interface card (NIC) driver for the xv6 operating system. The driver supports packet transmission and reception, allowing xv6 to communicate over a network.

 ## Project Structure
@@ -6,5 +7,6 @@
 - `src/driver/nic.c`: Implementation of the NIC driver.
 - `src/driver/nic.h`: Header file for the NIC driver.
 - `src/netif.c`: Network interface functions.
 - `src/netif.h`: Header file for network interface functions.
 - `include/nic_iface.h`: NIC interface definitions and constants.
 - `patches/patch-xv6-add-nic.diff`: Patch for integrating the NIC driver into xv6.
 - `tests/functional/netlab.c`: Functional tests for the NIC driver.
 - `tests/scripts/run-tests.sh`: Script to run functional tests.
 - `qemu/qemu-run.sh`: Script to run xv6 with QEMU.
 - `docs/design.md`: Design document for the NIC driver.
 - `Makefile`: Build instructions for the project.
 - `.gitignore`: Git ignore file.
 - `README.md`: Project documentation.

## Setup Instructions
1. Clone the repository.
2. Run `make` to build the project.
3. Use `qemu/qemu-run.sh` to run the xv6 operating system with the NIC driver.

## Usage
The NIC driver can be used to send and receive packets through the xv6 networking stack. Functional tests are provided to verify the driver's functionality.

